<title>POLAND: Bank Zachodni net rises to PLN 118 mln in 1996.</title>
<headline>Bank Zachodni net rises to PLN 118 mln in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's state-owned Bank Zachodni SA, slated for privatisation in 1998, had a net profit of 118 million zlotys last year against 111 million in 1995, the bank said in a statement on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Zachodni, one of Poland's 10 largest banks, had a pre-tax profit of 204 million zlotys last year, up from 179 million.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
